# Efficiency

`AGENTS.md` is already in context. Do not read it again.

Before editing, open the source and tests for the behavior you are changing, and the one "What to open" row that matches the task. Skip the other rows. Read `README.md` only when the public contract or quick start changes. Read `docs/STATUS.md` only when recorded status changes. Load one research note when the task needs it.

Do not read `docs/archive/` into context except for a citation, a contradiction, or provenance. Do not read files under `graphify-out/` into context. Graphify is optional: one focused `query`, `path`, or `explain` when a cross-file trace helps. Do not run it before every file read.

Run the `AGENTS.md` check sequence when source, tests, configs, or schemas change. Skip it for a documentation-only or Cursor-configuration edit.
